<title>USA: Columbia/HCA employees subpoenaed - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Columbia/HCA employees subpoenaed - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>At least four employees of Columbia/HCA Healthcare Corp have been subpoenaed to testify before a grand jury, the Wall Street Journal said.</p>
<p>In Monday's electronic edition, the paper said a Columbia spokeswoman confirmed that the employees were subpoenaed, but declined to disclose the offices they worked in or their areas of responsibility.</p>
<p>The subpoenaes could be a prelude to indictments in the federal probe of the company's billing practices, the article said.</p>
<p>The investigation is focused on possible Medicare fraud and could last 18 months or longer, Wall Street analysts have said.</p>
</text>
